{
  "dom_id": "step-q186855",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Complete the ratio table below.\n\n| $4$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $16$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $20$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $28$ | {{field-3}} |",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:1$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($4$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($1$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $16,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 4}{1\\times 4}=\\frac{16}{4}\n$$\n\n- To create a numerator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{20}{5}\n$$\n\n- To create a numerator of $28,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 7}{1\\times 7}=\\frac{28}{7}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $4$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $16$ | $4$ |\n| $20$ | $5$ |\n| $28$ | $7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
